{"name":"Sweet Cherry","hex":"#9f4f4d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet cherry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Prunus avium","Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see sweet,‎ cherry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet_cherry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prunus avium","blocks":[{"text":"Prunus avium, commonly called wild cherry, sweet cherry or gean, is a species of cherry, a flowering plant in the rose family, Rosaceae. It is native to western Eurasia and naturalized elsewhere. It is an ancestor of P. cerasus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Prunus_avium_fruit.jpg/330px-Prunus_avium_fruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunus_avium"},{"title":"Sweetness","blocks":[{"text":"Sweetness is a basic taste most commonly perceived when eating foods rich in sugar. Sweet tastes are generally regarded as pleasurable. In addition to sugars like sucrose, many other chemical compounds are sweet, including aldehydes, ketones, and sugar alcohols. Some are sweet at very low concentrations, allowing their use as non-caloric sugar substitutes. Such non-sugar sweeteners include saccharin, aspartame, sucralose and stevia. Other compounds, such as miraculin, may alter perception of sweetness itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Strawberry_shortcake.jpg/330px-Strawberry_shortcake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetness"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry"},{"title":"Cerise (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Cerise is a dark pink shade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Bandyball1.jpg/330px-Bandyball1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerise_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/01_Prunus_sp..jpg/500px-01_Prunus_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/01_Prunus_sp..jpg/1280px-01_Prunus_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/01_Prunus_sp..jpg/500px-01_Prunus_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Prunus avium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A01_Prunus_sp..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Glandes_Prunus_avium.jpg/500px-Glandes_Prunus_avium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Glandes_Prunus_avium.jpg/1280px-Glandes_Prunus_avium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Glandes_Prunus_avium.jpg/500px-Glandes_Prunus_avium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red glands (extrafloral nectaries) on the petiole","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlandes_Prunus_avium.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/0_Prunus_avium_-_Havr%C3%A9_%281%29.JPG/500px-0_Prunus_avium_-_Havr%C3%A9_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/0_Prunus_avium_-_Havr%C3%A9_%281%29.JPG/1280px-0_Prunus_avium_-_Hav